# Prospective algorithm timing and isolated memory

This is a separate readiness stage for the frozen 88-artifact algorithm candidate. Candidate entry SHA-256 `225a47ad0c6e089c67ce591013797b20a876630132af2b8060f9380afed3ed53` and helper `de334c498bb286c640661d8a3df05794fb66ebb02a3629231f18dbcb3c9bd58c` are copied exactly. Baseline stays `9269cf8c32be9bf2c075b67019e82e41272d9495f0321fefc17b2c5695a91371`. Authentic original @grafana/data 13.2.3 uses its five actual CJS files plus resolved Lodash 4.17.23, both original archive SHA-256/SHA-512 identities and Node 24.16.0 Windows x64 executable identity. Original module copies are evidence only; authentic original code is loaded only in verification/measurement children. The production application never loads it.

The previous seven workload specifications, generator, seeds, input files, fresh result/cache packets, complete-cache rereads, subset-cache rereads, metadata hash, warmups, iterations, transient loops and retained result counts remain exact. They are small standard, large standard, single p95, all percentiles, all calculations, independently constructed p95 and organ-pipe p95. The additional 66-input fixture is authenticated correctness provenance only and is not substituted into or added to this fixed measurement corpus. No thresholds or input selection are changed after seeing measurements.

Each sequence has three roles, seven workloads and seven repetitions: 147 fresh child executions. Role orders rotate as in the preceding control. Timing and memory require separate explicit coordinated root quiet timestamps after the new manifest date; completing one does not authorize the other. Root and other agents should pause tests/builds/browser activity/publication/source scans until the relevant window is explicitly closed. Unrelated Windows/background work remains uncontrolled; this is not machine-level isolation. No timing, memory or profiling workload is executed during readiness.

Timing retains the prior worker and measured loop exactly. All three implementations load in each timing child for common metadata/fresh/cache correctness prevalidation; only the selected role's loop is timed. Therefore timing memory/CPU diagnostics include common startup/prevalidation and are not an isolated memory comparison. Seven per-role samples, medians, min/max ranges, overlapping ranges, signed per-repetition candidate-minus-baseline/original differences, regressions and every raw child result remain visible. Bounds stay 60 seconds per timing child, 2 MiB child capture, 600 seconds outer timing controller, and 4 MiB outer capture. Those process controls differ from the separate memory limits and must not be conflated.

Isolated memory retains the prior memory worker, observer and measured operation/GC/checkpoint bodies exactly. Each child loads exactly one reducer implementation: original six CJS files, baseline one native ESM module, candidate its two native ESM modules. A matching owned-PID observer must produce a sample before the parent sends `start\n`; observation is nominally every 100 ms. This matches a numeric PID, not a process start-time identity; reuse could affect a late sample. The limits remain 120 seconds per child, 256 MiB old space, 512 MiB observed/checkpoint RSS and 4 MiB stdout/error/observer capture. A failed/limit-hit child aborts the remaining sequence; actual partial/failed samples are preserved and treated as censored, never filled or silently retried. Small spikes between polls may be missed. Logical RSS checks and process kill cannot promise instantaneous OS enforcement, whole-process-tree control or machine resource isolation. The memory controller has no separate outer watchdog; its child timers and observer cleanup are the retained controls, while scheduling reservations are estimates.

Memory retains separate lifetime peak RSS, polled RSS peak and checkpoint RSS, never substitutes one for another. Selected import/init, shared input, warm base, transient blocks, retained-after-GC and released-after-GC snapshots remain distinct. Retained-minus-before-retention heap, released-minus-warm-base heap, checkpoint/import changes and candidate-minus-baseline/original paired differences remain signed without clipping negative values. GC and allocator state can make negative differences valid observations. Each retained output is serialized with complete-cache and subset-cache rereads after its retained snapshot and before release/GC. Temporary validation allocations are dropped, but resulting allocator capacity/RSS may persist. Release measurements are diagnostics, not standalone leak proof or allocation attribution.

Only harness guard tests and correctness-only preflights are allowed now: one fresh calculation plus two cached rereads for each fixed input per implementation. There are no measured warmups, transient/retention loops, memory snapshots, observer execution or profiles in that branch. Invalid timestamp guards must reject before workloads. The exact full/held-out/adversarial candidate acceptance and root independent review are reused as finite compatibility provenance; no new 2.9-million correctness replay is claimed.

Source snapshots and before/after fingerprints include both candidate modules, unchanged baseline, all actual original loaded files, original archive identities, generator/canonical serializer, process controllers, workers, observer source and manifest. Every output/input fixture is authenticated. Native registry metadata, fresh result/cache object graphs, complete/subset reads, sparse holes, signed zero and shared aliases are part of the packet contract. Candidate source, old measured studies, fixed fixtures and production must remain unchanged through every future sequence. Failed branch execution, partial output, censoring and original errors will be retained.

`summary.mjs` fixes pure prospective signed-delta and censoring rules, verified against synthetic observation objects only. Missing pairs/checkpoints remain visible; a zero control permits a signed difference but no percentage. Its tests execute no reducer/process/resource work. Any future actual consolidation must authenticate raw logs and process outcomes independently before applying those rules.

One preparation attempt resolved the archive parent one directory too shallow and failed before creating the manifest. Its exact source and observed tool-console error copy are preserved under `failures/archive-parent-path`; the copy is explicitly not described as an automatic raw child capture. The corrected preparation verifies the six already created evidence files unchanged. No candidate, worker or measured loop changed because of this failure.

Scheduling reservations are conservative estimates: 5–8 minutes for timing and 10–15 minutes for isolated memory, with separate windows. The preceding rejected-control sequences actually took 100.064 and 264.904 seconds; those observations provide scheduling context only and do not predict the new candidate's performance. Future execution can fail on branches not exercised by readiness. Root reviews readiness and supplies each fresh authorization; this stage does not self-select, integrate or publish any candidate. Performance parity, universal correctness/superiority and full-product gates remain false.
